<section id="faq"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sh rv"><span class="eyebrow">Questions</span><h2>Straight <span class="grad">answers</span>.</h2></div>
  <div class="faq rv">
    <details open><summary>What is MatchBox?</summary><p>MatchBox is a Rust implementation of the BoxLang runtime. BoxLang is the platform, and it now has two runtimes: the JVM runtime and MatchBox on Rust. MatchBox compiles BoxLang to bytecode and runs it on a Rust VM with a tiered JIT in the native CLI.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is MatchBox a replacement for BoxLang on the JVM?</summary><p>No. It complements it. Use the JVM runtime for the full Java ecosystem and broad module coverage. Use MatchBox to run BoxLang where a JVM does not fit, such as single binaries, the browser, WASI containers, serverless and microcontrollers. Runtime APIs and module support differ, so check compatibility for your target.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does MatchBox need a JVM?</summary><p>No, not for the core runtime or for native builds. Experimental Java interop exists in native builds and needs a JDK on the machine.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where can MatchBox run?</summary><p>Native executables, the browser and JavaScript (including Cloudflare Workers), WASI containers, AWS Lambda (preview) and ESP32 devices.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I install it?</summary><p>Install MVM, the MatchBox Version Manager, then run <code>mvm install latest &amp;&amp; mvm use latest</code>. See the <a href="#variables.basePath#getting-started/installation/">installation guide</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can AI agents write MatchBox code?</summary><p>Yes. Install the BoxLang skills with <code>npx skills add ortus-boxlang/skills</code> and your agent learns the targets, commands and limits. This site also publishes an llms.txt index and an MCP endpoint.</p></details>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="final" id="install"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">Start in a minute</span>
  <h2 class="rv">Start with a script. <span class="grad">Ship a binary.</span></h2>
  <p class="rv">Install MVM, pick a MatchBox version, run a file, then build it for the target you need.</p>
  <div class="cta rv"><a class="btn p" href="#variables.basePath#getting-started/quick-start/">Quick start &rarr;</a><a class="btn" href="#variables.basePath#getting-started/">Read the docs</a></div>
  <div class="install rv"><code><span class="pr">$</span> mvm install latest &amp;&amp; mvm use latest</code><button type="button" data-copy="mvm install latest && mvm use latest">Copy</button></div>
</div></section>


